						"value": "RENDERING\n\nAs we discussed in the previous section, shapes are not pixels.\nTo turn them into pixels we use the Shape Render node.\nThis node converts the Shape 2D type into a Texture2d RGBA type.\nDo note that the rendering of a shape is a destructive process, it is not possible to convert textures back into shapes.\n\nWhile rendering you can assign a color to the shape as demonstrated in the first example below.\n\nAssignment: change the color of the first example to a semi-transparent one.\n\nIn the second example we use the Antialiasing settings on the shape render to get a more smooth\/blurred render of the shape.\n\nAssignment: play around with both the In and Out directions of the Shape Render as well as the amount of AA."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 917.9920654296875,
					"width": 964.87384033203125,
					"x": 979.71624755859375,
					"y": 422.990478515625
