					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "SHAPE OPERATIONS\n\nWe can use the shape nodes \"as is\" , but there is more fun to be had with the special shape operations in Wire.\n\nUnion can be used to combine multiple shapes and smooth between them.\nSubtract can be used to subtract multiple shapes from each other and smooth them.\nEdge can be used to extract the edge from a shape.\nAnd that is just the tip of the iceberg, there are shape operations like Displace, Distance Lines, Intersection, Repeat and Exclude for you to explore.\n\nAssignment: Explore the shape category and the shape nodes to create a true shape monstrosity (skip the Polygon node for now, we'll get back to that later)."
					}
				},
